h a blank category cell instead of being rejected.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-24\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Deleting a category that is actively in use by transactions is not blocked and does not require reassignment; it silently orphans the affected transactions' category field.\", \"actual\": \"Deleting the &quot;Travel&quot; category (which had 1 transaction assigned, &quot;Business Trip - Conference&quot;) was allowed without being blocked and without prompting for reassignment. The confirmation dialog only states &quot;Transactions using this category will not be deleted&quot; as a generic warning (shown identically even for a 0-transaction category). After confirming deletion, the transaction row for &quot;Business Trip - Conference&quot; now shows a blank/empty category cell instead of &quot;Travel&quot;, leaving an orphaned reference with no reassignment step.\", \"evidence\": \"Before deletion, transaction &quot;Business Trip - Conference&quot; had category &quot;Travel&quot;. After deleting Travel category via Delete confirmation, the same transaction row reads &quot;Nov 20, 2024 Business Trip - Conference TRIP-001 -$1,250.00 ✓&quot; with no category text present.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-16\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"After adding an income (+$999) and expense (-$123.45) transaction dated in the current month (Aug 2026), Dashboard immediately showed Monthly Income $999, Monthly Expenses $123, Net Profit/Loss $876, and both transactions appeared at top of Recent Transactions, without any manual refresh.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-17\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Edited &quot;QA IX18 CT21 Test Expense&quot; (initially not tax-related) via Edit Transaction dialog, toggled the &quot;Tax Related&quot; switch on, and saved. The transaction table immediately showed a ✓ in the Tax column. Navigating to Tax Summary for 2026 (previously $0.00 across the board) now showed Total Deductible Expenses $150.00, Net Taxable Income -$150.00, a Marketing $150.00 (100%) row in Deductible Expenses by Category, and the transaction listed in &quot;All Tax-Related Transactions&quot; (1 transactions).\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-18\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Before adding a new transaction, Marketing category showed &quot;1 transactions&quot; / Total $850. After creating a new $150 expense transaction assigned to the Marketing category, the Categories page immediately reflected &quot;2 transactions&quot; / Total $1,000 (850+150) without any page reload.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-19\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Clicking &quot;Print Report&quot; on the Tax Summary page did not throw any new console errors or crash the page (console error/warning count remained unchanged before and after the click: 1 pre-existing unrelated React key-prop warning, 5 warnings). Page remained fully rendered and interactive after the print action.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-20\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Transaction table displays all expected fields (Date, Description, Category, Reference, Amount, Tax) for each row. Footer shows Total Income +$47,592.50 and Total Expenses -$36,485.99 for the full unfiltered result set; manually summing all displayed income rows (42.50+1800+8750+5500+3500+15200+12800=47,592.50) and expense rows (54.99+850+156+12500+285+2200+1250+3600+2200+890+12500=36,485.99) both match exactly.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-21\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"After adding a $150 expense dated Aug 24, 2026 (current month) with no income transactions this month: Monthly Income shows $0, Monthly Expenses shows $150, Net Profit/Loss shows -$150 (0-150), and Recent Transactions list shows the new &quot;QA IX18 CT21 Test Expense&quot; entry at the top with correct category (Marketing), date (Aug 24, 2026), and amount (-$150.00). All figures are internally consistent and accurate.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-22\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Chart axis labels lack precision for values under $500\", \"actual\": \"Income vs Expenses chart Y-axis gridlines, scaled to a max of ~$999, displayed \\\"$0k\\\" for two different non-zero gridline levels (e.g. 0 and ~$250) in addition to zero, formatted only in whole $k units so amounts below $500 are indistinguishable from $0.\", \"evidence\": null}]}"
